 "notes": [
  "Parts are the same as step 1; no changes.",
  "Each speaker connects to Uno pins 6, 7 and 8 in turn, per the sketch. Each signal runs from the Uno pin through a jumper wire and a 100 ohm resistor to the speaker. The other speaker lead goes to the ground rail.",
  "The ground wire goes from the Uno GND to the top rail (tn). I assumed that is the ground rail, as the image shows.",
  "Breadboard columns (9, 16, 23) and rows are my choice, since the image doesn't give exact holes. Each resistor spans the centre gap, and the speaker lead shares the resistor's top-half column.",
  "Speaker leads are symmetric, so lead 1 goes to the resistor side and lead 2 to ground. The image shows the red lead to the resistor and the black lead to the rail.",
  "The schematic image did not render, so the circuit image is the only wiring reference."
